{
  "duration": 365.71200000001113,
  "chapters": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 132.4080000000041
    },
    {
      "start": 132.4080000000041,
      "end": 289.46400000000915
    },
    {
      "start": 289.46400000000915,
      "end": 365.71200000001113
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 0.7599999904632568,
      "text": "Welcome back.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 1.3200000524520874,
      "end": 5.676535682415399,
      "text": "In this class we will work through first law signs, isothermal and adiabatic",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.676535682415399,
      "end": 8.600000381469727,
      "text": "derivations, path dependence and second law limits.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 9.239999771118164,
      "end": 13.9399995803833,
      "text": "If systems A and B are each in thermal equilibrium with C, they are in thermal",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 13.9399995803833,
      "end": 15.239999771118164,
      "text": "equilibrium with one another.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.859999656677246,
      "end": 19.65666720806024,
      "text": "This zeroth law idea makes a thermometer meaningful: it can compare",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 19.65666720806024,
      "end": 20.280000686645508,
      "text": "temperature",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20.280000686645508,
      "end": 23.3799991607666,
      "text": "after reaching equilibrium without measuring every molecule.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 24.299999237060547,
      "end": 26.020000457763672,
      "text": "Temperature is not the amount of heat stored.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 26.719999313354492,
      "end": 30.6200008392334,
      "text": "Heat names energy transferred because of a temperature difference, while",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 30.6200008392334,
      "end": 32.880001068115234,
      "text": "internal energy is a state property of the system.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 33.7599983215332,
      "end": 35.31999969482422,
      "text": "Choose work by the gas as positive.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 36.13999938964844,
      "end": 40.459999084472656,
      "text": "The first law then reads the change in internal energy equals Q minus work by",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 40.459999084472656,
      "end": 40.86000061035156,
      "text": "the gas.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 41.900001525878906,
      "end": 46.36000061035156,
      "text": "Heat entering is positive Q; expansion work is usually positive work by the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 46.36000061035156,
      "end": 48.279998779296875,
      "text": "gas, while compression work is negative.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 49.31999969482422,
      "end": 54.619998931884766,
      "text": "If 500 J enters and the gas does 200 J of work, internal energy increases by",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 54.619998931884766,
      "end": 55.36000061035156,
      "text": "300 J.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 55.779998779296875,
      "end": 59.953075849092926,
      "text": "The sign convention must be stated because another text may use work on the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 59.953075849092926,
      "end": 60.119998931884766,
      "text": "gas",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 60.119998931884766,
      "end": 60.560001373291016,
      "text": "instead.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 61.459999084472656,
      "end": 65.33999633789062,
      "text": "For an ideal gas with fixed composition, internal energy depends on",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 65.33999633789062,
      "end": 68.80000305175781,
      "text": "temperature, so equal endpoint temperatures give equal endpoint internal",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 68.80000305175781,
      "end": 69.23999786376953,
      "text": "energies.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 70.33999633789062,
      "end": 74.12000274658203,
      "text": "The work done by a gas against its surroundings is the integral of external",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 74.12000274658203,
      "end": 75.4800033569336,
      "text": "pressure with respect to volume.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 76.19999694824219,
      "end": 80.46923006497897,
      "text": "On a mechanically quasistatic path the gas pressure is arbitrarily close to",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 80.46923006497897,
      "end": 80.63999938964844,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 80.63999938964844,
      "end": 84.58000183105469,
      "text": "external pressure, so the plotted equilibrium P V curve can be used.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 85.45999908447266,
      "end": 89.55999755859375,
      "text": "A constant pressure expansion gives the rectangular area P the volume change.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 90.27999877929688,
      "end": 94.4923087878105,
      "text": "An isochoric step has zero volume change and therefore zero boundary work,",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 94.4923087878105,
      "end": 94.72000122070312,
      "text": "even",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 94.72000122070312,
      "end": 95.72000122070312,
      "text": "when pressure changes.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 96.81999969482422,
      "end": 102.80000305175781,
      "text": "Take endpoints A at 0.001 cubic metres and 100000 Pa, and",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 102.80000305175781,
      "end": 107.69999694824219,
      "text": "C at 0.002 cubic metres and 200000 Pa.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 107.69999694824219,
      "end": 112.91999816894531,
      "text": "Expand first at 100000 Pa, then raise pressure at constant volume: work is 100",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 112.91999816894531,
      "end": 113.12000274658203,
      "text": "J.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 113.94000244140625,
      "end": 118.5999984741211,
      "text": "Raise pressure first, then expand at 200000 Pa: work is 200 J.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 119.66000366210938,
      "end": 123.73999786376953,
      "text": "The endpoints and the change in internal energy are the same, but Q differs by",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 123.73999786376953,
      "end": 124.37999725341797,
      "text": "100 J.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 125.22000122070312,
      "end": 126.55999755859375,
      "text": "Heat and work are path quantities.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 127.30000305175781,
      "end": 130.56666917067307,
      "text": "Do not use an endpoint pressure in P the volume change when the actual",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 130.56666917067307,
      "end": 130.94000244140625,
      "text": "pressure",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 130.94000244140625,
      "end": 132,
      "text": "changes along the path.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 132.4080000000041,
      "end": 136.4080000000041,
      "text": "For a fixed amount of ideal gas held at constant absolute temperature T,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 137.06799984741622,
      "end": 141.3479995803874,
      "text": "equilibrium pressure is nRT/V.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 141.3479995803874,
      "end": 144.92235888730974,
      "text": "Integrate this pressure from initial to final volume on a reversible",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 144.92235888730974,
      "end": 145.44799996185714,
      "text": "isothermal",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 145.44799996185714,
      "end": 145.88799954224044,
      "text": "path.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 146.8479995803874,
      "end": 151.30799961853438,
      "text": "Since nRT is constant, work by the gas is",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 151.30799961853438,
      "end": 154.498000152592,
      "text": "nRT",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 154.498000152592,
      "end": 157.68800068664962,
      "text": "ln(V_final/V_initial).",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 157.68800068664962,
      "end": 161.14799977112227,
      "text": "Expansion has a positive logarithm; compression has a negative one.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 161.5280008392375,
      "end": 166.04799938965255,
      "text": "The result needs the ideal gas and reversible or quasistatic isothermal model,",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 166.70799923706466,
      "end": 170.06799984741622,
      "text": "not just an arbitrary process whose endpoints happen to have the same",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 170.06799984741622,
      "end": 170.46800137329512,
      "text": "temperature.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 171.36799908447676,
      "end": 176.33723208383824,
      "text": "Ideal gas internal energy is unchanged, so the first law gives Q equals work",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 176.33723208383824,
      "end": 176.46800137329512,
      "text": "by",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 176.46800137329512,
      "end": 177.72799969482833,
      "text": "the gas.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 177.72799969482833,
      "end": 181.6679983215373,
      "text": "Isothermal does not mean no heat transfer: heat must enter during reversible",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 181.6679983215373,
      "end": 183.42800045776778,
      "text": "expansion to maintain temperature.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 184.1580000000041,
      "end": 189.20799923706466,
      "text": "For one mole at 300 K expanding from V to 2V, use R equals",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 189.20799923706466,
      "end": 194.9880018310588,
      "text": "8.314 and ln 2 equals 0.693.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 194.9880018310588,
      "end": 198.86799908447676,
      "text": "Work and heat are approximately 1729 J.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 198.86799908447676,
      "end": 203.56800366211348,
      "text": "In contrast, ideal gas free expansion into an insulated vacuum has zero",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 203.56800366211348,
      "end": 207.80800152588301,
      "text": "external pressure work and zero heat, but is irreversible even though its",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 207.80800152588301,
      "end": 209.68799877930098,
      "text": "temperature remains unchanged in this model.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 210.36799908447676,
      "end": 213.5880003051799,
      "text": "Adiabatic means Q equals 0.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 213.5880003051799,
      "end": 219.5880003051799,
      "text": "For a reversible adiabatic ideal gas process, n C V dT equals P",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 219.5880003051799,
      "end": 221.20800305176192,
      "text": "dV.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 221.20800305176192,
      "end": 225.68799877930098,
      "text": "Substitute P equals nRT/V and divide by T: C V",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 225.68799877930098,
      "end": 230.76800061035567,
      "text": "dT/T equals R dV/V.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 230.76800061035567,
      "end": 234.5079984741252,
      "text": "If heat capacities are constant, integrate to obtain T V^(R/C V)",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 236.80800152588301,
      "end": 237.16800213623458,
      "text": "constant.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 237.9080000000041,
      "end": 243.56800366211348,
      "text": "Because C P minus C V equals R and gamma equals C P/C V, the exponent",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 243.56800366211348,
      "end": 244.84800244141036,
      "text": "is gamma minus one.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 245.70800305176192,
      "end": 249.74799633789473,
      "text": "Combining with the gas law gives P V^gamma constant.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 250.5079984741252,
      "end": 254.20800305176192,
      "text": "For a monatomic ideal gas gamma is 5/3.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 254.20800305176192,
      "end": 260.187998779301,
      "text": "Doubling the volume lowers temperature to T_initial divided by 2^(2/3), so",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 260.64800549316817,
      "end": 264.24799633789473,
      "text": "300 K becomes about 189 K.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 264.24799633789473,
      "end": 268.5779981689494,
      "text": "Its adiabatic work is n C V(T_initial",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 268.5779981689494,
      "end": 270.4479932861369,
      "text": "T_final).",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 270.4479932861369,
      "end": 273.1079969482463,
      "text": "Energy comes from internal energy, not incoming heat.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 273.9479932861369,
      "end": 278.0680036621135,
      "text": "Irreversible adiabatic processes need the first law and actual external work;",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 278.5279951171916,
      "end": 282.2080030517619,
      "text": "the reversible P V^gamma relation cannot be assumed.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 283.04799938965255,
      "end": 286.96799755859786,
      "text": "Constant heat capacities are an additional model condition, not a promise for",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 286.96799755859786,
      "end": 289.26800061035567,
      "text": "every real gas over every temperature range.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 289.46400000000915,
      "end": 294.7840001716705,
      "text": "After a complete cycle the system returns to its initial state, so net the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 294.7840001716705,
      "end": 299.80400015259704,
      "text": "change in internal energy is zero and net Q equals net work by the gas.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 300.4439995422455,
      "end": 306.0040009155365,
      "text": "On a P V diagram a clockwise quasistatic loop usually represents positive work",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 306.0040009155365,
      "end": 309.58400083924255,
      "text": "by the gas; the enclosed signed area gives that work.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 310.5040009155365,
      "end": 316.224000228891,
      "text": "For a rectangular loop between volumes 0.001 and 0.002",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 316.224000228891,
      "end": 322.0839989318939,
      "text": "cubic metres and pressures 100000 and 200000 Pa, clockwise work is",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 322.0839989318939,
      "end": 324.20400167847595,
      "text": "100 J.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 324.20400167847595,
      "end": 326.04400183106384,
      "text": "Reversing the cycle reverses the sign.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 326.96400000000915,
      "end": 330.62399984742126,
      "text": "The second law prevents a cyclic engine from converting heat from a single",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 330.62399984742126,
      "end": 333.8240006103607,
      "text": "reservoir entirely into work without other effects.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 334.7639992370697,
      "end": 339.9840004577728,
      "text": "A reversible Carnot engine between reservoir temperatures T_hot and T_cold has",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 339.9840004577728,
      "end": 344.56399847413024,
      "text": "maximum efficiency 1 T_cold/T_hot, using kelvin.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 345.20400167847595,
      "end": 350.1840012207123,
      "text": "At 600 K and 300 K the limit is 50 percent.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 350.1840012207123,
      "end": 354.3039963378998,
      "text": "A real engine is less efficient under the same two reservoir conditions.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 355.56399847413024,
      "end": 359.10297519234814,
      "text": "Reversibility requires no entropy production and no finite gradient",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 359.10297519234814,
      "end": 359.6840012207123,
      "text": "dissipative",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 359.6840012207123,
      "end": 364.7240021362396,
      "text": "transfer; merely running a process slowly does not remove friction or make it",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 364.7240021362396,
      "end": 365.0239975586029,
      "text": "reversible.",
      "chapter": 2
    }
  ]
}
